text:
Jordan M.: Quick note from QA: onboarding sample app treats any non-2xx as `ApiError` and shows "Something went wrong" to users. This is killing developer UX for auth and rate limits.

Lina P.: Ouch. Do we have a spec that maps HTTP -> error.code + retry_hint? I can't find a single canonical table in docs.

Raj S.: There's a terse section but it's inconsistent. I've seen 429 return no Retry-After header and SDK still surfaces generic message. We should standardize to return machine fields: `error.code`, `error.http_status`, `error.retry_after` (optional), `error.human_message`, `error.dev_message`.

Jordan M.: Agree. Example proposal for error.code values: `auth_expired`, `invalid_auth`, `rate_limited`, `conflict`, `bad_request`, `server_error`, `network_transient`. Keep codes stable across SDKs.

Lina P.: For frontend UX: prefer short `human_message` like "Session expired, sign in again." or "Hit rate limit, try in a few seconds." and put details + request id in `dev_message`.

Raj S.: Implementation note: in JS SDK throw `RedwoodError` subclasses with `code` enum and `toJSON()` returning fields above. In Python raise subclasses with same attributes. Sample snippet for JS: 
```
class RateLimitError extends RedwoodError {
  constructor(resp){
    super('rate_limited', resp.status, resp.headers['retry-after'])
  }
}
```

Jordan M.: Also add SDK-level mapping rules: 401 -> `invalid_auth` (retry=false), 403 -> `forbidden` (retry=false), 429 -> `rate_limited` (retry=true if Retry-After present else conditional), 409 -> `conflict` (retry=false), 5xx -> `server_error` (retry=true). Document edge cases like 502/504 vs 500.

Lina P.: Telemetry: please emit `error.code`, `http_status`, `retry_expected` boolean and `request_id`. Current telemetry only logs message text which is useless for alerts.

docs-bot: docs PR template created: docs/error-mapping-guidelines.md (#402).

Raj S.: Testing plan: unit tests for SDK mapping, integration test that stubs responses (401/429/503) and asserts exception class + JSON fields, and a sample app end-to-end to show proper UI copy.

Jordan M.: UX quickstart change: update `examples/quickstart` to catch typed errors and show `human_message`. Pseudocode: 
```
try{
  await client.generate(...)
}catch(err){
  if(err.code === 'invalid_auth') showLogin();
  else showToast(err.human_message || 'Try again');
}
```

Lina P.: I'll draft the human_message examples and a small mapping table for docs. Raj, you want to own the SDK changes?

Raj S.: Yup, I'll take JS and coordinate on Python with Evan next week. I'll open a JS PR with types + tests.

Jordan M.: I'll own the quickstart updates and add a tiny CI check that runs the sample app against mocked failures.

